    "text": "Implementation contract (SHORT):\n\n- Requirement -> owning files:\n  - All active requirements (0–20) are implemented in game/flappy_bird_clone.py (game/__init__.py is empty package marker).\n- State ownership and interfaces:\n  - Bird state: flappy_bird_clone.py variables bird_x: int, bird_y: float, bird_vy: float, bird_rect: pygame.Rect.\n    - flap() -> None: sets bird_vy = FLAP_VELOCITY and prints \"FLAP\".\n    - update_bird(dt: float) -> None: applies gravity and integrates bird_y.\n  - Pipes state: list[dict] each with keys x: float, gap_y: int, scored: bool.\n    - spawn_pipe() -> dict: returns a new pipe dict appended to pipes list.\n    - update_pipes(dt: float) -> None: decrements x by PIPE_SPEED*dt.\n  - Score: integer score in module-level variable; increment when pipe passes bird_x and not scored.\n  - Game state: boolean running and game_over flags in module-level variables.\n- Input -> action -> state -> visible feedback:\n  - KEYDOWN Space -> flap() -> bird_vy set negative -> bird moves up next frames -> print \"FLAP\".\n  - KEYDOWN R -> reset() -> score=0, pipes cleared, bird reset -> print \"RESTART\".\n  - KEYDOWN Escape -> quit game -> print \"QUIT\".\n  - Collisions or out-of-bounds -> set game_over True, print \"GAME OVER\" and stop movements.\n  - All drawing occurs each frame: sky-blue background, bird sprite drawn at fixed x, pipes drawn moving left, score in top-left, GAME OVER + final score centered when ended.\n- Coordinate convention: top-left origin (0,0). y increases downward. Bird x is fixed at BIRD_X = 100.\n- Lifecycle: init -> play loop -> on game_over freeze updates -> on R restart resets all state -> Escape quits.\n- Files to write: game/__init__.py and game/flappy_bird_clone.py\n\nI will now write the two promised files.",
